  // Not from the source doc's own "Tag Snippet Presence & Location" item —
  // that one only tests something homepage-only crawl access can already
  // all-but-guarantee passes once GTM is confirmed connected at all (the
  // original install is rarely touched again), so it added a critical slot
  // with near-zero real chance of catching anything. Replaced with a
  // distinct, extremely common real-world failure that IS checkable from
  // this worker's actual GTM API access and genuinely fails often: a GA4
  // Configuration tag's default auto-pageview (sendPageView) left on
  // alongside a separate manual GA4 Event tag also sending page_view — a
  // subtle default-behavior trap most non-expert setups fall into,
  // precisely because it isn't obvious the config tag already covers it.
  // crawl.structuralSignals.gtmScriptEarlyInHead/gtmNoscriptRightAfterBody
  // still exist (computed in crawl.ts, surfaced in the prompt) as
  // unscored informational context, just no longer a scored checklist item.
